  "script": {
    "title": "Why Action Precedes Motivation",
    "category": "educational",
    "music_mood": "calm",
    "scenes": [
      {
        "narration": "We usually wait for motivation before taking action, but neuroscience shows the brain works in reverse.",
        "on_screen_text": "Action comes before motivation",
        "search_query": "person sitting desk thinking",
        "fallback_query": "person sitting chair"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Movement actually triggers motivation, not the other way around.",
        "on_screen_text": "",
        "search_query": "tying running shoe laces",
        "fallback_query": "tying shoe"
      },
      {
        "narration": "When your body starts a task, dopamine releases in response to progress.",
        "on_screen_text": "Dopamine follows progress",
        "search_query": "hands typing on keyboard",
        "fallback_query": "typing laptop"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Psychologists call this behavioral activation.",
        "on_screen_text": "Behavioral activation",
        "search_query": "writing notebook pen",
        "fallback_query": "hand writing"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Even moving for two minutes alters your brain chemistry.",
        "on_screen_text": "Just two minutes",
        "search_query": "stopwatch ticking hand",
        "fallback_query": "clock ticking"
      },
      {
        "narration": "You do not need to feel ready to begin; beginning makes you ready.",
        "on_screen_text": "Begin before you feel ready",
        "search_query": "person walking outdoors morning",
        "fallback_query": "walking path"
      }
    ],
    "caption": "Waiting until you feel like doing something often guarantees it will never get done. \n\nIn psychology, behavioral activation shows that physical action comes first, and the emotional feeling of motivation follows. Starting a tiny physical step signals your brain that work is underway, kicking off dopamine release.\n\nWhat is one small step you can take today without waiting to feel ready?",
